/*************************************************************************************
 *  ARTIPLAY — GOOGLE APPS SCRIPT BACKEND (v2 — single source of truth)
 *
 *  RULE OF THIS FILE: if the UI shows a number, a name, a status, or a list —
 *  it came from a sheet, computed here. The frontend (Index.html) holds ZERO
 *  hardcoded player/coach/session/message/reward content. It only renders
 *  whatever clientGetFullState() / clientGetCoachState() return, and calls a
 *  mutation endpoint for every user action. If you add a UI element that shows
 *  data, add the field to one of these two payloads (or a dedicated getter) —
 *  never hardcode it client-side.
 *
 *  SHEETS (auto-created by initializeDatabase()):
 *   MEMBERS, STAFF, LEVELS, BYTESENSE_SCORES, ATTENDANCE, ATTENDANCE_LOG,
 *   TRAINING_SESSIONS, SESSION_RSVPS, STORE_ITEMS, STORE_REQUESTS, REWARDS,
 *   POINTS_LEDGER, ACHIEVEMENTS, MEMBER_ACHIEVEMENTS, ACTIVITY, ACADEMIES,
 *   COACHES, MESSAGES, ANNOUNCEMENTS, AUDIT_LOG, SETTINGS, PARENTS,
 *   PARENT_CHILDREN, TENANT_INVITES
 *************************************************************************************/

